**Google Ads — conversions WoW (ad platform fixture, anchor 2026-10-30)**

**Absolute figures, both windows:**

| Metric | Prior week (Oct 17–23) | Last week (Oct 24–30) | Change |
|---|---|---|---|
| Conversions | 28 | 42 | +14 (+50.0%) |
| Spend | $5,377.43 | $8,029.35 | +$2,651.92 (+49.3%) |
| CPA | $192.05 | $191.18 | −$0.87 (−0.5%) |

**Direction:** Up — confirmed via `compare_windows` (28 → 42).

**Likely driver:** Conversions rose almost exactly in proportion to spend (+50.0% vs +49.3%), with CPA effectively flat. This looks like a **volume/scale story, not an efficiency story** — the account simply spent ~49% more and bought proportionally more conversions. No evidence of an efficiency improvement (CPA would have dropped) or degradation.

**Caveats:**
- Data is complete through 2026-10-30 for both windows, so no truncation issue.
- Conversion volumes are small (28–42/week), so a +50% swing is only ~14 conversions — wide uncertainty; don't over-read the percentage.
- Source is the ad platform (fixture), which is the correct source of truth for media metrics like conversions.
- Spend +49% WoW is a large budget move; worth confirming it was intentional before treating the conversion lift as organic performance.

